# Monitor security hardening

Root-privileged daemon paths must not trust world-writable directories, PATH lookups, or unrestricted env `dlopen`.

## Required contracts

| Area | Law |
|------|-----|
| Dump / stats dirs | Default dump under `/var/lib/hpcperfstats/dump` (not `/tmp`); create/validate via `ensure_private_dir(..., 0700)` |
| Append / create | `O_NOFOLLOW` (+ `O_CLOEXEC`); create mode `0600` (or tighter) — never `0666` |
| Daemon umask | Prefer restrictive `umask(0077)` after fork; do not rely on umask alone |
| Dumpfile list | Single-pass growable list with authoritative `out_n`; no precount/`calloc(n)` TOCTOU |
| DEBUG shm | `ensure_private_dir`; atomic writes `O_CREAT\|O_EXCL\|O_NOFOLLOW`; env dir only under `/dev/shm/` without `..` |
| Env `dlopen` | Gate overrides with `dyn_lib_path_allowed()` (`/usr/lib64/`, `/usr/lib/` absolute regular files; reject `..`); **non-empty disallowed override fail-closes** (do not fall back to defaults) |
| Child exec | Absolute `execv` paths (`/usr/sbin/beegfs-ctl`, `/usr/bin/xpumcli`, …); no `execvp` on PATH |
| `popen` | Absolute binary path in the command string; allowlist via `check_unsafe_c_patterns.sh` |
| BeeGFS cfg | `beegfs_path_is_safe` rejects `.` / `..` path components |
| Conf install | `hpcperfstats.conf` RPM install mode **`0600`** (holds broker secrets) |
| systemd unit (F6) | Shipped **`hpcperfstats.service`** must keep `PrivateTmp`, `ProtectSystem=strict`, `ProtectHome`, `ProtectKernelTunables`, `ProtectControlGroups`, `NoNewPrivileges`, `RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_UNIX AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_NETLINK`, `ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/hpcperfstats /run`; **do not** add `PrivateDevices=true` (IB/GPU/perf nodes). Do not remove sandbox keys without fleet justification; no in-process setuid-drop claims without a dedicated plan |

## Out of scope here

- **F12** default RabbitMQ sample credentials — won't-fix

